From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:30:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] decode attention: G6_ATTN_CTX3_SP=64|128 runs
 context_pk3 over 64- or 128-slot partitions (E1, default off)

The served context kernel (G6_ATTN_CTX3) is one CTA per (row, head group, 256-slot partition), and its time is
that CTA's serial chain over 256 slots. With G6_ATTN_CTX3_SP=64 (or 128) run_body's context_pk3 calls use
partitions of 64 (128) slots: 4x (2x) the CTAs, each a 4x (2x) shorter chain, and merge_parts sums the 32 (16)
partials in partition order. Every fmaf operand is unchanged; the 2048-slot fp32 sum is regrouped, so the
context differs in the last bits (E1), deterministically.

Only run_body (the replicated decode path) takes it; the CP calls keep 256-slot partitions and their merges.
The workspace sizes the partials for the flag. The flag is read once (before the bindings size their
scratch), is in the S2 runtime signature, and is off by default: with it off the kernels, grids and merges
are those of before (SP=256 is the old instantiation).
